1
00:00:02,402 --> 00:00:04,902
(Raj:)Have you guys seen this feature
that lets you talk to Siri

2
00:00:04,905 --> 00:00:06,635
(Raj:)without pressing
any buttons?

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,070
(Howard:)No. How does it work?

4
00:00:08,075 --> 00:00:11,515
You just say, uh, “Hey,
Siri, what time is it?”

5
00:00:11,512 --> 00:00:13,782
SIRI:
The time is 6:37 p.m.

6
00:00:13,781 --> 00:00:14,981
(Penny:)Yeah.

7
00:00:14,982 --> 00:00:17,212
(Howard:)So now anyone
can control your phone?

8
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:20,457
(Howard:)Hey, Siri, show me pictures
of naked grandma butts.

9
00:00:20,454 --> 00:00:22,184
(Raj:)Nice try.

10
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:25,389
It only recognizes my voice.
Oh. Cool.

11
00:00:25,392 --> 00:00:28,462
(imitates Koothrappali): Hey, Siri, show me
pictures of naked grandma butts.

12
00:00:28,462 --> 00:00:31,462
(Raj:)I don't sound
like that.

13
00:00:31,465 --> 00:00:35,335
SIRI: Here are some images
of naked grandma butts.

14
00:00:35,335 --> 00:00:37,735
(Sheldon:)Hey. Good news,
everybody.

15
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:40,008
(Sheldon:)Now that I'm no longer
with Amy,

16
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:42,937
(Sheldon:)I have an extra ticket to the
annual Thanksgiving lunch buffet

17
00:00:42,943 --> 00:00:45,613
(Sheldon:)at the aquarium cafeteria.
Who wants it?

18
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,150
(Sheldon:)Well, you realize
you won't be going alone...

19
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,820
(Sheldon:)I'll be there the whole time.

20
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,622
(Sheldon:)Providing
fish and pilgrim facts.

21
00:00:57,056 --> 00:00:59,626
(Sheldon:)Can you people hear me?

22
00:00:59,626 --> 00:01:01,396
(Leonard:)Well, we're having
everyone over.

23
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:03,164
(Penny:)Yeah, Leonard and I
are gonna be cooking

24
00:01:03,163 --> 00:01:05,563
(Penny:)all day.
Otherwise we'd love to.

25
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,735
(Penny:)But we can't.

26
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,663
(Leonard:)Yeah, poor us.
Mm-hmm.

27
00:01:11,136 --> 00:01:12,706
(Bernadette:)And Raj and I
are volunteering

28
00:01:12,706 --> 00:01:15,036
(Bernadette:)at the soup kitchen,
feeding food to the homeless.

29
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:17,211
(Sheldon:)Well, Howard,
what about you?

30
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:18,440
(Howard:)Oh...

31
00:01:18,445 --> 00:01:21,345
(Howard:)I can't. I'm going
to the soup kitchen, too.

32
00:01:21,347 --> 00:01:25,087
(Bernadette:)You said that sounded like
the worst thing ever.

33
00:01:26,585 --> 00:01:28,585
(Howard:)If you can't support me
when I'm lying,

34
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:31,388
(Howard:)why are we married?

35
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:34,761
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

